  "notes": [
    "The anchor is the first invest with an unlisted end_date, which made the stale reward immediately claimable. The attacker's earlier 1,000 ORT stake 0xa578e08c only probed the pool: its stale reward stayed locked for 730 days and was never claimed. The previous implementations had the same defect; the upgrade still resets (rule 9).",
    "Campaign: every tx emitting Invest with end_date 0 or an unlisted duration, or Claim on such a lock, from the attacker (0x9bbd9450) and four copycat senders, plus the attacker's four large 24-month stakes that raised total_percent. The stale total_percent itself is a live value, not a reset.",
    "Minted ORT had no market beyond the ORT/WBNB pair the sellers drained, so loss is what they realised (rule 15): the pair's WBNB outflow in the 48 sale txs from the five exploiting senders. WBNB the attacker spent buying ORT it then locked is not netted."
